            "review_title": "Review at Mr. Ya Bon Cafe",
            "review_text": "DirtyPierreOnTour\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12577 contributions\n0\nTook a Canadian friend to Thao Diem and needed lunch.\nMar 2018 • Friends\nWas showing my Canadian friend the French supermarket in Thao Diem in D2 and needed a quick place for lunch. On my last visit I only ate downstairs but this time we went upstairs and what a great find. They have both an open air area or an enclosed aircon area. Being expat fatties we chose the aircon. They have a lunchtime menu with specials for 159k which includes a main course, dessert and a drink.\nI chose a smoked salmon salad and my friend chose spaghetti Bolognese. We both had crepes for dessert.\nGood value lunch in pleasant surroundings.\nTasty food served by friendly staff.\nI can certainly recommend this place for lunch either alone or with friends.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 2, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
